unidpp demo service           # B5     edge state, freshness
unidpp demo derestrict        # B6     identity-changing modification
unidpp demo repair            # B7     regulated child swap
unidpp demo auction           # B8     custody, theft predicate, stamps
unidpp demo recall            # B9     predicate recall across the graph
unidpp demo recycle           # B10    decompose, end of waste
unidpp demo cub               # V1–V5  the counterpoint thread`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The E8 story"
  description="One e-bike — the Momiji Mobility E8, built in Kyoto from German and Chinese parts — walks the complete regulated lifecycle: assembly, part duties, EU placement, offline border verification, service, derestriction, repair, auction, recall, and end-of-life. A 1962 Super Cub is the counterpoint."
  eyebrow="Reference — the exemplar thread"
  sectioned
>
  <Sidebar slot="rail" heading="The E8 story" items={storyNav} />
  <h1>One e-bike, ten beats</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The canonical UniDPP narrative threads every product through one primary example —
    the Momiji Mobility E8, a Kyoto-built e-bike with a German drive unit and a
    Shenzhen battery pack — and one counterpoint, a 1962 motorcycle that adopts the
    system with no manufacturer, no applicable regulation and no connectivity behind
    it. Each beat states what happens, what the framework does, how it differs from a
    passport implemented as a rewritable document, and which repository carries it.
  </p>

  <section id="example" class="plate" aria-labelledby="example-h">
    <h2 id="example-h">Why an e-bike</h2>
    <p>
      The e-bike exercises six mechanisms simultaneously, to a degree that no other
      single product class reaches. The battery is a component under a mixed-profile
      regime: the EU Battery Regulation attaches passport duty to LMT batteries, while
      the vehicle itself answers to machinery and EPAC rules and, in Japan, to
      road-traffic law. Software determines the legal class: an EPAC is defined by its
      assistance cutoff (250&nbsp;W, 25&nbsp;km/h, EN&nbsp;15194), so a firmware update
      or an aftermarket device changes the legal identity of the vehicle. E-bikes form
      the most frequently stolen class of consumer goods in EU cities, which gives the
      resale beat an operational predicate. Edge state is native to the product and
      stratified across one product line: a silent frame, a logging battery-management
      system and a connected module. The sequence of Japanese placement, EU placement,
      resale and export reflects trade reality rather than staging. The lithium pack
      finally carries a UN&nbsp;3171 transport profile, which exercises the
      characteristic axis: a predicate-triggered profile that is neither a jurisdiction
      nor a sector.
    </p>
    <DataTable
      columns={['Entity', 'Identity', 'Notes']}
      rows={[
        ['<strong>E8 instance</strong>', '<code>momiji:e8/J-000842</code>', 'JP placement 2027-04; EU placement 2028-02'],
        ['<strong>E8 type + version</strong>', '<code>momiji:e8/type/2027.1</code>', 'a 2028.1 hardware revision exists (type-version visibility)'],
        ['<strong>Drive unit (EU)</strong>', '<code>rhine:du/M-771…</code>', 'Rhine Drives DE; type-level passport + EU DoC; installed R3'],
        ['<strong>Battery pack (CN)</strong>', '<code>weilian:wp/P-9904…</code>', 'Weilian, Shenzhen; 40 cells of Haichuan lot <code>haichuan:cell/H-2231</code> — dormant identifiers'],
        ['<strong>Charger (CN)</strong>', 'cert <code>CQC-2026-1142…</code>', 'GB 4943.1-2022 ≈ IEC 62368-1 (registered equivalence)'],
        ['<strong>Controller / BMS (JP)</strong>', 'device key, class S2', 'firmware vector in instance facts'],
        ['<strong>Connect module (optional)</strong>', 'device key, class S3', '<code>fresh_within</code> bounded'],
        ['<strong>Owners</strong>', '1st Düsseldorf · 2nd Vienna (auction)', 'custody edges, blind by default'],
        ['<strong>The 1962 Super Cub</strong>', '<code>cub:1962/S-00317</code>', 'the counterpoint thread'],
      ]}
    />
    <p>
      The problem of unreachable origins is concrete in this cast: the pack's data
      resides at the host of Weilian in Shenzhen; the Japanese host of Momiji serves an
      EN 18222-style REST interface, the Chinese consumer layer serves the GB/T 33993 QR
      platform, and the automotive community uses AAS. The settlement is not that every
      participant adopts a single protocol. It is one identity (L0); resolver linksets
      that route per context; foreign protocols served as renders through gateway
      adapters; equivalence claims expressed as registered transforms; and trust
      established under SIGNATIF cross-recognition. Each participant retains its
      protocol, and no participant's protocol constitutes the envelope.
    </p>
    <figure class="fig">
      <img
        src="/story/01-overview-system.svg"
        alt="Diagram: the E8 across five planes — carrier, resolver, neutral core passport, event log, and the registry and trust rails."
        width="960"
        height="540"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        The system in one picture: one e-bike across five planes and two rails — carrier,
        resolver, neutral core, event log, with the FERIN registry and SIGNATIF trust
        rails alongside.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="arc" class="plate" aria-labelledby="arc-h">
    <h2 id="arc-h">The story arc</h2>
    <p>
      Ten beats, 2027–2033: assembly, part duties, EU placement, the border moment,
      service, derestriction, repair, auction, recall, end of life. Every repository
      product earns its place in this sequence — no product exists that the story does
      not exercise.
    </p>
    <figure class="fig">
      <img
        src="/story/02-story-arc.svg"
        alt="Diagram: the ten beats of the E8 story as a grid of cards, each naming its mechanism and the repositories that carry it."
        width="960"
        height="540"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        The story arc: ten beats of one e-bike, B1–B10, each card naming its mechanism
        and its repositories.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  {
    beats.map((beat) => (
      <section id={beat.id} class="plate beat" aria-labelledby={`${beat.id}-h`}>
        <h2 id={`${beat.id}-h`}>
          <span class="beat-num">{beat.num}</span>
          {beat.title}
        </h2>
        <p class="kicker">{beat.kicker}</p>
        <p class="narr" set:html={beat.body} />
        <div class:list={['figs', { pair: beat.figures.length > 1 }]}>
          {beat.figures.map((f) => (
            <figure class="fig">
              <img
                src={`/story/${f.src}`}
                alt={f.alt}
                width="960"
                height="540"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption set:html={f.caption} />
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="meta carried" set:html={beat.carried} />
      </section>
    ))
  }

  <section id="counterpoint" class="plate" aria-labelledby="counterpoint-h">
    <h2 id="counterpoint-h">Counterpoint — the 1962 Super Cub</h2>
    <p>
      The e-bike exercises the regulated case at its most demanding. The vintage
      motorcycle exercises the opposite boundary and thereby the universality of the
      core: an object with no living manufacturer, no applicable regulation and no
      connectivity, which adopts the system <em>voluntarily, because provenance
      constitutes its commercial value</em>. The counterpoint comprises five beats:
    </p>
    <DataTable
      columns={['Beat', 'What happens']}
      rows={[
        ['<strong>V1</strong> — Commissioning', 'No living issuer: the auction house acts as qualified attestor and commissions identity <code>cub:1962/S-00317</code> (EPCIS commissioning semantics; nullable type reference).'],
        ['<strong>V2</strong> — The clock predicate', 'The historic-vehicle class binds when the object crosses the age threshold — a time-fired applicability event no human declares; the dated-binding machinery does it alone.'],
        ['<strong>V3</strong> — Attribution and restoration', 'Competing scholarly facts ("original paint" vs "respray, 1980s, documented") coexist with precedence rules, never merges; conservation events append exactly like repairs.'],
        ['<strong>V4</strong> — The theft flag', 'Stolen 1987, recovered 2024: a title taint as a graph event, attached by authority; history is never rewritten.'],
        ['<strong>V5</strong> — Value is a verdict', 'Condition and appraisal stamps under different lenses (auction vs insurance), dated and signed — the native form for anything whose worth is judged, not measured.'],
      ]}
    />
    <figure class="fig">
